{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-point-of-sale-basic-tapi-integration-make-a-payment-greece-tax","reason":"The independently computed SHA-256 matches the trusted input, and a full read of the pinned raw supports the dated Greek scope, Terminal API and firmware gates, merchant POS/provider/terminal/AADE handoff, conditional autonomous mode, refund distinctions, and the unexplained EUR 10 requested versus EUR 8 authorized Success examples. All five quotes are exact at their cited lines; the reciprocal Terminal API route and most locators resolve. Two narrow material qualifications are missing from the retained signature guidance. First, the Errors table explicitly rejects a verification timestamp in the future as well as one older than 24 hours, while the candidate and fixed answer 2 state only the age limit; a future-dated signature could be selected as valid from those summaries and then fail. Second, the raw says not to send aadeProviderSignature in any other request than the payment request but later instructs the POS to send the returned signature to its e-invoicing system; the candidate's unqualified 'used only in the payment request' sits beside its provider-result handoff and implies a global prohibition that the page itself does not resolve. The signed-flow AdditionalResponse instruction should also be scoped to that flow, since the autonomous Success example does not show those fields. These bounded corrections leave the raw, route, and reciprocal source link unchanged; company and index promotion remain coordinator-owned."}
{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-point-of-sale-tipping-tipping-on-receipt","reason":"Full independent review of the SHA-256-matched pinned raw found one material qualification broadened from authorization adjustment to the whole receipt-tipping flow. The two paths, backend endpoints and references, total-amount semantics, webhook outcomes, 0-20% scheme range, wallet/debit exclusion, and chargeback warnings otherwise match the raw. All five quotes and detail locators are accurate, both fixed retrieval answers are sound, and the two proposed reciprocal routes are relevant."}
